 "answer": "Yes, the haze in KL is bad right now. The air quality is in the \"unhealthy\" range.\n\n**Latest readings (evening of 16 Oct):**\n- In Kuala Lumpur, Batu Muda and Cheras both recorded an API of 163, while Putrajaya registered 170.\n- Earlier in the week, Cheras hit 174. The Vibes reported Cheras at 174 and Batu Muda at 163.\n- Nearby areas are worse. Shah Alam recorded 181, Petaling Jaya 170.\n- Nationwide, Pasir Gudang in Johor reached a very unhealthy 202 at 5.30pm.\n\n**What the numbers mean:** 101 to 200 is unhealthy, 201 to 300 is very unhealthy, and above 300 is hazardous. KL is in the upper-middle part of the unhealthy band and is not yet in the very unhealthy range.\n\n**What to do:**\n- Limit strenuous outdoor activity.\n- Wear an N95 mask if you have to be outside.\n- Keep windows closed. Use an air purifier if you have one.\n- Children, older people, and people with asthma, heart or lung conditions should be especially careful.\n\nThe readings change hourly. For the current figure, check the Department of Environment's APIMS or a tracker such as semakapi.my.",
